id: pm-2zkvxm
title: Workspace history integrity refusals escape typed CLI recovery and become high Sentry faults
description: "A verified workspace-history chain mismatch is a deterministic tracker-integrity refusal with existing recovery commands, but five SDK paths throw raw TypeError. During the broad SDK acceptance, a deliberate before_hash mismatch therefore surfaced as PM-CLI-35 / unclassified_runtime_error instead of a stable machine-readable conflict diagnostic."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:cli","area:history","area:sdk",error-taxonomy,integrity,sentry
created_at: "2026-08-15T22:45:17.608Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T00:12:45.786Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-16T00:12:45.055Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-16T00:12:45.055Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "All workspace-history chain verification refusals share one typed PmCliError contract with a stable code, exact verifier evidence, and executable recovery guidance.; CLI, SDK, and mutation callers receive conflict semantics without capturing deterministic integrity refusal as an unexpected Sentry fault; unrelated unexpected errors remain fail-closed.; Tests cover every workspace-history verifier call site plus a real CLI mutation negative control, and full exact coverage remains 100/100/100/100."
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: 95
severity: high
environment: pm-cli 2026.8.15; Node v26.5.0; isolated manual acceptance on Linux
repro_steps: "Create an isolated tracker with a workspace history entry, alter its before_hash, then run any audited singleton mutation; observe exit 1 and pm.error_code=unclassified_runtime_error."
resolution: "All workspace chain verification boundaries now emit typed conflict code workspace_history_chain_invalid with exact verification_errors and executable recovery across SDK, CLI JSON, classification, and display surfaces."
expected_result: A corrupt workspace audit chain refuses all affected reads and writes through one structured conflict envelope that points to history verification and repair.
actual_result: "Five raw TypeError branches are replaced by one SDK-owned PmCliError; real isolated CLI corruption exits 4 with structured evidence; 7,398 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass."
fixed_version: next daily release after 2026.8.15
component: "core/history/workspace-history, CLI error transport, Sentry reliability gate"
customer_impact: "Corrupt workspace state is correctly refused but agents cannot classify or execute recovery from the raw runtime error, and the release reliability gate treats the expected refusal as an unexpected product fault."
